  "complexity": 4,
  "title": "E6v2: acceptance gate v2: every acceptance path that looks like a test file (any language) must exist and be in the task diff",
  "spec": "Goal T-1403, wave 2, plan label E6v2 (refile of T-1507; content unchanged). Evidence: luna T-0104 passed the gate without backend/test/oauth.test.ts and google-oauth.test.ts although its acceptance named them (plan.md backlog); fix rounds are 41% of execute runs, partly missing non-Python acceptance tests (analysis finding 5).\n\nFacts (goal/T-1403; acceptance.py and the daemon gate unchanged since main 355583c; re-check daemon.py line numbers on the current goal branch, B2a T-1504 has merged since):\n- orchestrator/acceptance.py:8-11 _TEST_ID only matches tests/<...>.py::name; named_tests() (23-37) and missing_tests() (52-66) check that the named Python function is defined. Non-Python paths are never checked.\n- orchestrator/daemon.py gate() (~1437-1450): after the dirty-scope check, missing = acceptance.missing_tests(...); non-empty -> stamp gated_at, hold gate_red with resume_hint {'failures': ['FAILED path::name (missing: ...)'], 'missing_tests': missing}, gate_reds += 1, and skip the gate run.\n- daemon.py:26-27 changed_paths(task) wraps gitutil.changed_paths (diff base..HEAD names, None when unavailable).\n- tests/test_daemon.py:161 patches daemon.acceptance.missing_tests; most daemon gate tests use acceptance like ['pass'] with no test-file path, so the new check returns [] for them.\n\nChange:\n1. acceptance.py: test_file_paths(acceptance) -> sorted unique paths from whitespace tokens (strip surrounding quotes, backticks, brackets and trailing ':,;.'): skip tokens containing '*' or ending in '/'; drop tokens containing '::' whose left side ends in '.py' (missing_tests owns those); for other '::' tokens use the left side. A token is a test file when it has a file extension and either a path component is exactly 'test', 'tests' or '__tests__', or the file name matches *.test.<js|jsx|ts|tsx|mjs|cjs>, *.spec.<same>, *Test.swift, *Tests.swift, *Test.kt, *Tests.kt, *Test.java, *Tests.java. '.claude/hooks/tests-green.sh' must not match. missing_test_files(worktree, acceptance, changed=None) -> paths that are not files under worktree, or (when changed is a list) not in changed.\n2. daemon.gate(): compute files = acceptance.missing_test_files(worktree, acceptance, changed_paths(t)) next to the existing missing_tests call; when either list is non-empty, one gate_red hold whose failures list holds the existing lines plus 'FAILED <path> (missing: test file not in task diff)' per file and resume_hint gains 'missing_test_files': files. Same stamp/gate_reds/_hold_stale_high handling as today; no second code path.\n3. roadmap.py's missing_tests call is unchanged.\n\nTests that assert the old behaviour (SPEC RULE): tests/test_acceptance.py tests (13-75) pin Python-id behaviour and must pass unchanged; tests/test_failures.py (~32-39) parses 'FAILED ... (missing: test not defined)' lines, keep that text for Python ids. Run tests/test_acceptance.py, tests/test_failures.py and tests/test_daemon.py.\n\nWork on the task branch cut from goal/T-1403. Commit first, then run the focused tests in the foreground; never background a command and never run the full gate. Write tests as unittest.TestCase methods using tests/_harness.py like the neighbouring tests. Locate every insertion point by symbol, never by line number. Every test named in the acceptance must exist in the diff; the gate checks for them by id.\n\nRe-filed 2026-10-02 10:40 (replaces T-1507): B2b T-1506 is parked after five spec-review rounds; depends_on re-pointed to the merged B2a T-1504; spec, acceptance and scope unchanged.",
  "inputs": [],
  "acceptance": [
    "tests/test_acceptance.py::test_missing_test_files_requires_test_paths_in_diff: passes: acceptance.test_file_paths() extracts backend/test/oauth.test.ts, web/src/a.spec.ts, apple/AppTests/FooTests.swift, android/app/src/test/BarTest.kt and tests/test_x.py (bare, no ::) but not tests/test_x.py::test_y (handled by missing_tests), .claude/hooks/tests-green.sh, globs or directories; missing_test_files(worktree, acceptance, changed) returns those absent from the worktree or not in changed (changed None -> existence only)",
    "tests/test_daemon.py::test_gate_holds_when_acceptance_test_file_missing_from_diff: passes: daemon.gate holds a done execute task gate_red with resume_hint.missing_test_files and a 'FAILED <path> (missing: test file not in task diff)' failure line, without running tests-green, when its acceptance names backend/test/oauth.test.ts that the task diff does not contain",
    ".claude/hooks/tests-green.sh wt/THIS-TASK exits 0"
  ],
